+\subsection{Unresolved Answer-Equivalence Caveat}
+\label{sec:caveat}
+B17--20 display both requested recent assessment means within supported personal-change claims. The frozen focal predicate recognizes comparison panels/claims but misses these visible means. B remains 15/24 visible and 14/24 selected complete in the frozen outcomes. Crediting only these four forms gives 19/24 visible complete, below the target; selected completeness stays 14/24 because grade context is compiler supplied. This conditional calculation is not independent adjudication.
+
+C21/C23 display earlier/recent means in peer claims without an explicit personal-change answer; equivalence is a separate question. All 96 slots are prepared for two independent human reviewers and adjudication, but no ratings exist. The requested two-reviewer validation remains outstanding; frozen completeness is not a settled measurement construct.
